        "original_id": "1aa361ae-42e6-55d4-89ca-b0290eed7553",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- TV Series: Joe Bash, Barney Miller, The X-Files\n- People: Peter Boyle, Danny Arnold\n- Organizations: New York City Police Department\n- Roles: beat cop, TV producer\n- Awards: Emmy Award\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: acting career, television production\n\nFacts:\n- In 1970, Peter Boyle had a breakthrough performance in the film \"Joe\".\n- After his breakthrough in \"Joe,\" Peter Boyle won praise in both comedic and dramatic roles.\n- Danny Arnold created the TV series \"Joe Bash\" after the success of his New York City police detective sitcom \"Barney Miller\".\n- \"Joe Bash\" starred Peter Boyle as a weary and embittered New York City Police Department beat cop.\n- In 1996, Peter Boyle won an Emmy Award for a guest-starring role on the science-fiction drama \"The X-Files\".",
